{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 10.092,
   "text": "In the little town where I grew up, there's an old swing set in the park... and every kid there knows the rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.692,
   "end": 14.34,
   "text": "If a swing is moving on its own... never push it."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.34,
   "end": 20.673,
   "text": "My grandmother used to say it like a prayer. Because if you push it... it pushes back."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.473,
   "end": 27.511,
   "text": "I moved away at eighteen. Last fall, after she died, I came home to empty out her house."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.211,
   "end": 31.923,
   "text": "The shortcut from the store cuts right through that park."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.523,
   "end": 37.003,
   "text": "One night, there was no wind at all... but the middle swing was moving."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.003,
   "end": 42.419,
   "text": "Back... and forth. Back... and forth. A little higher every time."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.319,
   "end": 47.095,
   "text": "Then, from the empty seat, a small voice whispered..."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 48.295,
   "end": 49.249,
   "text": "Push me."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.649,
   "end": 55.553,
   "text": "I didn't. I walked home fast, and I never looked back."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 56.553,
   "end": 61.737,
   "text": "Around three a.m., a sound woke me. Grandma's porch swing... creaking."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.737,
   "end": 68.558,
   "text": "I opened the front door. The porch swing was empty... and perfectly still."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 69.958,
   "end": 74.182,
   "text": "Then two small, cold hands pressed flat against my back..."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 75.382,
   "end": 78.22,
   "text": "and a little voice said... my turn."
  }
 ],
